703 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 396 0 R
/E (Vineyard City has been awarded a grant of nearly $700,000 from the Utah Outdoor Recreation Division to help fund the construction of the All-Wheels Concrete Skatepark, an exciting new recreation project planned for the community.)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
704 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 396 0 R
/E (The 16,000-square-foot skatepark will be located just southeast of Vineyard City Hall. Construction is expected to be completed by the end of Summer 2027. The park will include a variety of features such as bowls, rails, stairs, mini ramps, curbs, quarter pipes, and more, designed to accommodate skateboarders, scooter riders, BMX riders, rollerbladers, and adaptive athletes of all ages and skill levels.)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
705 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 396 0 R
/E (In addition to the skate features, the project will include trail connections, expanded parking, seating areas, bike racks, landscaping, restrooms, signage, and utility infrastructure to support potential future lighting around the park. Future Phase 2 improvements may include an asphalt pump track, outdoor lighting, and a shade structure, with opportunities for future fundraising support for these enhancements.)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
